            <div xml:id="d687">

                <pb facs="0513" n="509" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg509"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/3710: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hong Kong</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Southard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hong
                                Kong</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-22T21:00:00+08:00">October 22, 1938—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 22—5 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to your telegram of October 19, 10 [<hi rendition="#italic">11</hi>]
                        a.m.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d687-f1"/> about American-born Chinese on
                    Shameen. I have talked with the British Ambassador who asks me to tell you that
                    he is immediately taking the matter up by telegraph and will help all he can but
                    is not in a position to say what the decision may be.</p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking, Canton. Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Southard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
